    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986, by its Section 3401(a)(1), requires the Commission to assess and collect fees and annual charges in any fiscal year in amounts equal to all of the costs incurred by the Commission in a fiscal year. For the purposes of recovering this payment, this Section establishes a FERC ACA Unit Charge to be applicable to all jurisdictional transportation quantities transported. These costs will continue to be recovered under its current rates with customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC 740 considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Company is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the recovery of costs associated with compliance to a final order (CPF No. 1-2018-1003) issued by the Pipeline and Hazardous Materials Safety Administration (PHMSA) regarding validation of maximum allowable operating pressure (MAOP) for certain pipeline segments in the state of Ohio.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the under recovery of costs under the &#8220;Operational Transaction Rate Adjustment (OTRA)&#8221;, a mechanism that ensures a sufficient amount of flowing supply to northern Ohio in accordance with FERC Docket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting. The regulatory liability will be amortized over varying terms that approximate the expected reversal of the underlying deferred tax assets and liabilities that gave rise to the regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Penalties collected during the year to be refunded to non-offending customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing donot represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes tracker activity that can be either overcollected or undercollected.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes sales in accordance with Respondent's Operational Transaction Rate Adjustment (OTRA) filing under FERCDocket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes sales in accordance with Respondent's Operational Transaction Rate Adjustment (OTRA) filing under FERCDocket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes sales in accordance with Respondent's Operational Transaction Rate Adjustment (OTRA) filing under FERCDocket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes volumes purchased in accordance with Respondent's Operational Transaction Adjustment (OTRA) filing under FERC Docket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes volumes sold in accordance with Respondent's Operational Transaction Adjustment (OTRA) filing under FERC Docket No. RP12-605.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Deliveries include, but are not limited to, flow tests, blowing drips, running pigs, removing freezes, blowing down lines, well construction, compressor station blowdowns, consumer taps, methanol line installation, heaters, products extraction, free gas, starts and stops, transportation retainage paid to third parties, and decreases in customer storage.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Retainage volumes reported by Respondent are actual volumes retained by contract type (Discounted, Negotiated, or Recourse.)</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent uses a monthly average spot rate as the basis for valuing gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent does not track Gas Used or Lost and Unaccounted For by contract type. Lines 9 through 29 are allocated between contract type (Discounted, Negotiated, and Recourse) using a pro-rata allocation calculated by the actual volumes retained by contract type.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Uses include, but is not limited to, flow tests, blowing drips, running pigs, removing freezes, blowing down lines and compressor stations, well construction, consumer taps, methanol line installation, heaters, products extraction, free gas, starts and stops, and transportation retainage paid to third parties.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Storage Other Use is comprised of calculated storage gas losses, which is also reflected in the Respondent's annual RAM filing. Volumes attributed to negotiated contracts include all wells that are part of a market based rate structure. Remaining volumes were allocated using the above allocation method.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent has a Commission approved Retainage Adjustment Mechanism (RAM) that recovers from its shippers system gas used and lost. Any excess or deficient balance is included in the next annual filing and collected or passed back, as appropriate, through a change in the surcharge.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accounts debited for Other Transmission Gas Uses include: 753, 756, 816, 817, 818, 820, 821, 825, 845.1, 852, 856, 857, 858, 859.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accounts debited for Other Transmission Gas Uses include: 753, 756, 816, 817, 818, 820, 821, 825, 845.1, 852, 856, 857, 858, 859.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accounts debited for Other Transmission Gas Uses include: 753, 756, 816, 817, 818, 820, 821, 825, 845.1, 852, 856, 857, 858, 859.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The incremental projects listed&#160; utilize the prevailing system fuel rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Adjustment are 2,383,219,377 Dth.</link:footnote>
